§9 A guide for making a        house a home!
#-   §9⛏*⋆§1Article Ω≠ƸӜ§9⋆*⛏
   §4ᴛʜᴇ ᴀʀᴛ ᴏꜰ ʟᴏʀᴇ
§8-------------------
§1Lore is a great way to make your build come to life when it is in fact nothing but some random blocks in a block game about blocks. Take Sweetpea, for example. Now she has a real problem with being LORE obsessed. Everything
#- §1she makes must have a deeper meaning or story behind it. A random tavern must have a backstory about a super secret witch cult. Every home must have a reason and have so many details it makes you think; do her builds have more life than she does in real life? Take this magazine as§r
#- §1yet another LORE filled project. She could have just made a normal book, like 'Craft Life' was once upon a time, but no, she had to add twists and turns at every page. She had to make a story within a story within a story. Many plot points and characters and secrets all mixed up§r
#- §1in a huge disaster pie that never ends. She is so invested in her own creation that she now has to make these mags just so she can peronally see what happens next. Who is §5ɨȶ§r? Even she doesn't §1'quite' know yet, she makes§r§5 ɨȶ§r up as she §1goes along! Pun intended. A Spotify Playlist (§oWitch-Craft§r)§r§r
#- §1that acts as the unoffical soundtrack!? I mean, who does that!?

Anyway, my point is, Sweetpea knows how to bring her virtual world to life and it's a skill that comes in handy when you want a silly block game to be so much more! Try it... it's very fun! ☻✍§r
#- §8-------------------
§9⛏§1I’ll try to be less 'meta' and get back to this reality in the next Crafty Witches!§9⛏
