✿✿❀❀❀✿✿.✿✿❀❀❀✿✿
✿✿❀❀❀✿✿.✿✿❀❀❀✿✿
§5 ⚜ ᴀ ꜱᴛᴏʀʏ ꜱᴇʀɪᴇꜱ ⚜
#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗  §2    ɴᴏ ᴇɴᴅ ɪɴ ꜱɪɢʜᴛ
§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§2Fern and Castien were both seasoned explorers. Castien was more of a mage than a warrior where as Fern was more of a warrior with far less experience with magic. Despite her witch mother and magical creation.§r 
#- §2A small part of her rebelled against the whole witchcraft thing. Castien was highly skilled in magic and was always on the lookout for the next big adventure. Fern, not so much. So when they stumbled upon 
a mysterious portal deep in an underground stronghold... well...§r
#- §2they couldn't resist the urge to jump through it! 

The legendary End they had heard stories about since they were children was far too intriguing. This was an opportunity that couldn’t be missed. Fern quite fancied the idea of slaying a§r 
#- §2dragon, and Castien quite fancied the chance to study a whole new dimension, that’s if the stories were even true.

As they leapt through the portal, they were shocked to find themselves separated and enveloped in darkness. They couldn't see a thing§r
#- §2and the only sound was the echo of their own footsteps. They tried calling out to each other, but their voices seemed to disappear into the void. They both soon realised that they had made a grave mistake. 

This was not The End, but somewhere else entirely.§r
#- §2Fern’s thought’s turned to §5ɨȶ §2and how they had led them here in the first place. Was this a trap? Had she fallen for this? As they both walked trying to find each other, they could feel §0The Darkness §2closing in on them, as if it was alive. They could sense something watching.
#- §2They quickened their pace, trying to find a way out. But §0The Darkness §2was unyielding. It seemed to have no end, no beginning. It was like they were trapped in an endless abyss. Suddenly, they heard a voice. It was faint, like a whisper on the wind, but it was definitely a voice.
#- §2They couldn't make out the words, but it sent shivers down their spines. They knew they had to find the source of the voice. As they walked, the voice grew louder and clearer. It seemed to be leading them somewhere. They followed it, their hearts pounding with fear and then§r
#- §2excitement when they found each other again. Nothing mattered for a brief moment as they embraced and held on tightly.

They soon found themselves in a large ruined chamber, the walls made out of a strange, pulsating black stone.§r
#- §2Almost invisible as it blended in with the dark around it. Fern could just about make out carvings of repeated numbers in the stone; §70010110§2. 
In the centre of the chamber stood a humanoid figure. 
It was shrouded in darkness, and they couldn't make out its features.
#- §2Like a shadow or imprint of a person long gone. But they could feel its gaze upon them. It glitched in and out for a fraction of a second and its head twitched leaving faint echoes of§r §5purple §2and §6gold §2glow behind.

The figure spoke in a language they did not
#- §2understand, but the tone was clear. It was a warning, a warning of something terrible to come. Fern and Castien realised that they had entered into a place not meant for them, or anything, a place not of this reality. They knew they had to find a way out before it was 
too late! 
#- §2They turned around to leave but found that where they entered the chamber was now blocked off. They were trapped! §0The Darkness §2closed in on them, and they could feel the presence of something ancient and malevolent. They knew then that they were doomed.
#- §2Fern and Castien never returned from that portal, their fate remains a mystery. Some say they were devoured by §0The Darkness§2, while others believe they are still trapped in that strange dimension, forever lost in the abyss. Unless some unlikely heroes can save them...
#- §2To be continued…
